      "text": "$NVDA today announces capacity agreements with substrate, packaging, testing and optical engine suppliers.\n\n- Substrate agreements with Ibiden, Samsung Electro-Mechanics and Unimicron to expand by 2.5x\n- $AMKR to increase advanced packaging capacity by more than 300% by the end of 2028, with a new $1.3B agreement\n- Multibillion dollar capacity reservation advance to support Ibiden's plant in Japan\n- \"By 2028, production allocated to $NVDA is projected to account for a significant portion of Samsung Electro-Mechanics' total annual package substrate production capacity\"\n- KYEC with $1.1B capacity reservation in advance\n- SPIL for optical engine capacity for CPO by 15x by H2 2027 and double that for 2028\n\nWell, that's a lot of news. As Jensen Huang puts it: \"Demand is extraordinary. Capacity is the constraint.\"",
